   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **People**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Lonely Woman**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Hot Pearl C**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Whatever It Is**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Romantic**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n- **Kalen**: rare: 11 archived performances [2]\n- **I Don’t Know What You Came To Do**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2002-04-12.akg480.ackerman.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 174 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- N'Dambi sang on the first three tracks, with Soulive acting as her backing band [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2002-04-12.akg480.ackerman.flac24**: taped by Ray Ackerman; transferred by Ray Ackerman / Dave Mallick; source: AKG480/ck61uls > Aerco MP-2 > Sony D-10 Pro II [1]. Also: Recorded with an AKG 480 microphone and ck61 ULS capsule, run through an Aerco MP-2 preamp into a Sony D-10 Pro II recorder; Transferred using Sound Studio 4.11.0 and xACT 2.58, then encoded to FLAC [1]",
